{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-7de4647e-019d-4afc-9fba-da2e780183be","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-97de50dbb08329b8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9013-zruidodm/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E001.md","content":"# KServe FIPS 140-3 image remediation and FIPS regression CI enforcement\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic makes the KServe model serving stack's own images — its control-plane\ncomponents and its serving data plane — run correctly on FIPS-enabled OpenShift\nclusters using validated cryptographic modules, with no non-validated crypto in\nthe request path. It also delivers the FIPS regression enforcement slice for\nKServe's builds: a gating CI check that fails any KServe serving-stack build\nreintroducing non-validated crypto usage. The epic produces the KServe portion\nof the module inventory, build attestations, and test results that the\nserving-stack compliance evidence package is assembled from.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Audit KServe's serving-stack images (control-plane components and the\n  serving data plane) to inventory non-validated cryptographic library usage,\n  with focus on the request path.\n- Replace non-validated crypto library usage with validated cryptographic\n  modules in those images.\n- Verify InferenceService deployment and request serving on FIPS-enabled\n  OpenShift clusters using validated crypto modules.\n- Preserve existing serving behavior on non-FIPS clusters (no functional\n  regression from the crypto module change).\n- Add a gating CI check on KServe serving-stack builds that fails any build\n  reintroducing non-validated crypto usage, and verify it fails a build that\n  reintroduces such usage.\n- Produce the KServe-images module inventory and FIPS test results for\n  consumption by the compliance evidence package.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The module inventory for all KServe serving-stack images is complete and\n  shows no non-validated cryptographic library usage in the request path.\n- Models deploy and serve inference requests correctly on a FIPS-enabled\n  OpenShift cluster using validated crypto modules.\n- Existing serving behavior on non-FIPS clusters is unchanged by the crypto\n  module replacement (no functional regression).\n- A gating CI check fails a KServe serving-stack build that reintroduces\n  non-validated crypto usage, and passes the remediated builds.\n- The KServe module inventory and FIPS test results are produced in a form\n  the compliance evidence package can consume.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)**: KServe's share of \"all serving-stack images run correctly\n  on FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules\" — the KServe\n  control-plane and serving data plane images.\n- **HLR-3 (P1, bundled)**: the CI FIPS-regression gating check for KServe\n  builds. Bundled with the P0 remediation because it is an enforcement\n  deliverable over the same surfaces being converted — it shares the builds\n  and module-inventory data with the remediation and has no independent user\n  value over unconverted builds.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":38630,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b901be51241a67d5","agent_id":"a5e7f9a0dee6eb09e","session_id":"58d4774e-cbd2-4ab5-97a3-4f58877fb394","uuid":"274096bf-03c6-4e39-95c6-56f1a5960e04","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:19:04.691Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9013"}
