{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-84f607ca63ad62ac","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E003\n3\ttitle: Serving-stack FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package and certification submission\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: KServe\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9013-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9013-E002\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 1\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: 0\n17\t  open_questions: 1\n18\t  external_dependency: -1\n19\t  human_process_gates: -1\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: Medium\n25\tai_implementability_score: 2\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# Serving-stack FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package and certification submission\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tThis epic assembles the FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package for the model\n36\tserving stack — module inventory, build attestations, and test results — and\n37\tsubmits it through the security review board to the external accredited\n38\tcertification laboratory. The package draws on the remediated KServe and\n39\tPlatform Operator images once their FIPS remediation is complete, so this work\n40\tstarts after those remediations finish.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Assemble the module inventory covering all serving-stack images (KServe\n45\t  control-plane, KServe serving data plane, and Platform Operator), reconciled\n46\t  against the final remediated image builds.\n47\t- Collect build attestations for the final serving-stack images.\n48\t- Compile the FIPS test results produced by the remediation work (cluster-level\n49\t  operation on FIPS-enabled OpenShift and per-image verification).\n50\t- Package the evidence and submit it through the security review board to the\n51\t  external accredited certification lab.\n52\t- Track the submission through review-board sign-off and lab acceptance into\n53\t  review.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- The module inventory covers every serving-stack image in scope and is\n58\t  reconciled against the final remediated builds (no stale or\n59\t  pre-remediation entries).\n60\t- Build attestations for the final serving-stack images are included in the\n61\t  package.\n62\t- FIPS test results demonstrating correct operation on FIPS-enabled clusters\n63\t  with validated crypto modules are included in the package.\n64\t- The complete evidence package is submitted through the security review\n65\t  board to the external accredited certification lab and accepted into the\n66\t  lab's review queue.\n67\t\n68\t## Risks / Notes\n69\t\n70\t- The accredited lab's turnaround is historically six to nine months and the\n71\t  security review board operates on its own cadence — both are externally\n72\t  controlled and cannot be compressed by engineering effort; they dominate\n73\t  the schedule regardless of engineering speed. The certification grant\n74\t  itself is outside this epic's deliverable, which ends at submission and\n75\t  acceptance into review.\n76\t- Public-sector deal timing depends on the certification outcome; plan\n77\t  commitments accordingly.\n78\t\n79\t## HLR Traceability\n80\t\n81\t- **HLR-2 (P0)**: \"A compliance evidence package (module inventory, build\n82\t  attestations, test results) is assembled and submitted through the security\n83\t  review board to the external certification lab.\"\n84\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-808c7f66d7e88190","agent_id":"a08eb07699e6b2531","session_id":"58d4774e-cbd2-4ab5-97a3-4f58877fb394","uuid":"3565805e-4754-4011-9aba-d0ec6cb2a23c","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:25:54.581Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-84f607ca63ad62ac","permission_decisio