{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f8bc51768720682","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E001\n3\ttitle: KServe FIPS 140-3 image remediation and FIPS regression CI enforcement\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: KServe\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# KServe FIPS 140-3 image remediation and FIPS regression CI enforcement\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic makes the KServe model serving stack's own images — its control-plane\n34\tcomponents and its serving data plane — run correctly on FIPS-enabled OpenShift\n35\tclusters using validated cryptographic modules, with no non-validated crypto in\n36\tthe request path. It also delivers the FIPS regression enforcement slice for\n37\tKServe's builds: a gating CI check that fails any KServe serving-stack build\n38\treintroducing non-validated crypto usage. The epic produces the KServe portion\n39\tof the module inventory, build attestations, and test results that the\n40\tserving-stack compliance evidence package is assembled from.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Audit KServe's serving-stack images (control-plane components and the\n45\t  serving data plane) to inventory non-validated cryptographic library usage,\n46\t  with focus on the request path.\n47\t- Replace non-validated crypto library usage with validated cryptographic\n48\t  modules in those images.\n49\t- Verify InferenceService deployment and request serving on FIPS-enabled\n50\t  OpenShift clusters using validated crypto modules.\n51\t- Preserve existing serving behavior on non-FIPS clusters (no functional\n52\t  regression from the crypto module change).\n53\t- Add a gating CI check on KServe serving-stack builds that fails any build\n54\t  reintroducing non-validated crypto usage, and verify it fails a build that\n55\t  reintroduces such usage.\n56\t- Produce the KServe-images module inventory and FIPS test results for\n57\t  consumption by the compliance evidence package.\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- The module inventory for all KServe serving-stack images is complete and\n62\t  shows no non-validated cryptographic library usage in the request path.\n63\t- Models deploy and serve inference requests correctly on a FIPS-enabled\n64\t  OpenShift cluster using validated crypto modules.\n65\t- Existing serving behavior on non-FIPS clusters is unchanged by the crypto\n66\t  module replacement (no functional regression).\n67\t- A gating CI check fails a KServe serving-stack build that reintroduces\n68\t  non-validated crypto usage, and passes the remediated builds.\n69\t- The KServe module inventory and FIPS test results are produced in a form\n70\t  the compliance evidence package can consume.\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\t- **HLR-1 (P0)**: KServe's share of \"all serving-stack images run correctly\n75\t  on FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules\" — the KServe\n76\t  control-plane and serving data plane images.\n77\t- **HLR-3 (P1, bundled)**: the CI FIPS-regression gating check for KServe\n78\t  builds. Bundled with the P0 remediation because it is an enforcement\n79\t  deliverable over the same surfaces being converted — it shares the builds\n80\t  and module-inventory data with the remediation and has no independent user\n81\t  value over unconverted builds.\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-808c7f66d7e88190","agent_id":"a