{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c5a8b8f44d4ee1c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E002\n3\ttitle: Platform Operator FIPS 140-3 image remediation and FIPS regression CI enforcement\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: Platform Operator\n6\tteam: RHOAI Platform\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 0\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Platform Operator FIPS 140-3 image remediation and FIPS regression CI enforcement\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic makes the Platform Operator's image(s) — the operator managing the\n34\tserving stack's deployment — run correctly on FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters\n35\tusing validated cryptographic modules, with no non-validated crypto in the\n36\trequest path. It also delivers the FIPS regression enforcement slice for the\n37\tPlatform Operator's builds: a gating CI check that fails any Platform Operator\n38\tbuild reintroducing non-validated crypto usage. The epic produces the Platform\n39\tOperator portion of the module inventory, build attestations, and test results\n40\tthat the serving-stack compliance evidence package is assembled from.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Audit the Platform Operator image(s) to inventory non-validated\n45\t  cryptographic library usage, with focus on the request/reconciliation path.\n46\t- Replace non-validated crypto library usage with validated cryptographic\n47\t  modules in those images.\n48\t- Verify the operator deploys and reconciles serving-stack resources correctly\n49\t  on FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters using validated crypto modules.\n50\t- Preserve existing operator behavior on non-FIPS clusters (no functional\n51\t  regression from the crypto module change).\n52\t- Add a gating CI check on Platform Operator builds that fails any build\n53\t  reintroducing non-validated crypto usage, and verify it fails a build that\n54\t  reintroduces such usage.\n55\t- Produce the Platform Operator module inventory and FIPS test results for\n56\t  consumption by the compliance evidence package.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- The module inventory for the Platform Operator image(s) is complete and\n61\t  shows no non-validated cryptographic library usage in the request path.\n62\t- The operator deploys and reconciles the serving stack correctly on a\n63\t  FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster using validated crypto modules.\n64\t- Existing operator behavior on non-FIPS clusters is unchanged by the crypto\n65\t  module replacement (no functional regression).\n66\t- A gating CI check fails a Platform Operator build that reintroduces\n67\t  non-validated crypto usage, and passes the remediated builds.\n68\t- The Platform Operator module inventory and FIPS test results are produced\n69\t  in a form the compliance evidence package can consume.\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- **HLR-1 (P0)**: Platform Operator's share of \"all serving-stack images run\n74\t  correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules\".\n75\t- **HLR-3 (P1, bundled)**: the CI FIPS-regression gating check for Platform\n76\t  Operator builds. Bundled with the P0 remediation because it is an\n77\t  enforcement deliverable over the same surfaces being converted — it shares\n78\t  the builds and module-inventory data with the remediation and has no\n79\t  independent user value over unconverted builds.\n80\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-959346b303c4f52a","agent_id":"ae